    [38;5;153mtoggleDone[39m, [38;5;153mdeleteTask[39m, [38;5;153mgetTasks[39m, and [38;5;153msubscribe(fn)[39m. Every mutation does three things in order: update state, append
    a change event, persist. Nothing else in the app touches [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m for tasks.
  - [1m[38;5;153msrc/storage.js[0m — the [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m boundary. [38;5;153mloadTasks[39m/[38;5;153msaveTasks[39m/[38;5;153mloadEvents[39m/[38;5;153mappendEvent[39m, plus JSON parse/serialize
    and a schema version field. This is the module you'd rewrite for IndexedDB or a server; nobody else knows storage
    exists.
  - [1m[38;5;153msrc/events.js[0m — the change-event log: shape, append, read, and the cap (keep the most recent 200; older ones fall
    off). Notifications will import from here and nothing else.
  - [1m[38;5;153msrc/ui.js[0m — renders the task list into [38;5;153m<main>[39m, wires the form and the per-task controls, re-renders on
    [38;5;153mstore.subscribe[39m. Plain DOM, no template library.

  [38;5;153mindex.html[39m stays a thin shell: the heading, a form, [38;5;153m<main>[39m, and one [38;5;153m<script type="module">[39m that boots the app.

  The dependency direction is one-way — [38;5;153mui[39m → [38;5;153mstore[39m → ([38;5;153mevents[39m, [38;5;153mstorage[39m) — so nothing below the store knows the DOM
  exists, and each module is testable on its own. When notifications arrive they become a fifth module reading [38;5;153mevents[39m
  and rendering into its own container; the store doesn't change.

