[1m[38;5;231mWhich tooling should we set up before writing code?[0m

  [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m Unit tests (Recommended)
  [38;5;246mA test runner plus a first passing test. The store and event log are pure logic — exactly the code worth testing, and
[39m  [38;5;246mTDD needs somewhere to put the test.[39m
[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m2.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m [38;5;153mLint + format (Recommended)[39m
  [38;5;246mESLint + Prettier with the standard config, run on demand. Catches typos in a no-build project where nothing else [39m
  [38;5;246mwould.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] End-to-end tests
  [38;5;246mPlaywright driving a real browser. Real confidence in the DOM layer, but a heavier dependency and slower runs for a [39m
  [38;5;246msingle page.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] None for now
  [38;5;246mPlain files only. Fastest to start; you verify by opening the page. Adding tests later is harder than adding them now.
